{"title":"Selle Royal Turns 70 with a See-Through Saddle and a Shrine to Failed Prototypes","link":"https://bikerumor.com/selle-royal-turns-70-with-a-see-through-saddle-and-a-shrine-to-failed-prototypes/","date":1795613340000,"content":"<p><img src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-side-top-e1795461635802.jpeg\" width=\"1000\" height=\"527\" alt=\"Selle Royal Nothing to Hide Saddle side top\" /></p>\n<p>Selle Royal just wrapped its “Nothing to hide” exhibition in London. It was a four-day pop-up that ran November 12-15 alongside Rouleur Live. It’s the centerpiece of the Italian saddle maker’s <a href=\"https://www.selleroyal.com/en-us/pages/70-anniversary\" target=\"_blank\">70th anniversary</a>. And yes, the theme is exactly what it sounds like: a brand airing its dirty laundry.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-pooh-e1795461673110.jpeg\"><img width=\"1024\" height=\"910\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-pooh-e1795461673110.jpeg\" alt=\"Selle Royal Nothing to Hide Saddle pooh\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-pooh-e1795461673110.jpeg 1024w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-pooh-e1795461673110-297x264.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-pooh-e1795461673110-120x107.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-pooh-e1795461673110-768x683.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-pooh-e1795461673110-1013x900.jpeg 1013w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The star of the celebration is a limited-edition Lookin Evo with a transparent cover that lets you see the saddle’s inner structure and materials. It’s a collector’s piece, but Selle Royal says it’s meant for actual riding. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-side.jpeg\"><img width=\"1000\" height=\"1000\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-side.jpeg\" alt=\"Selle Royal Nothing to Hide Saddle side\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-side.jpeg 1000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-side-297x297.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-side-120x120.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-side-768x768.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-side-900x900.jpeg 900w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-top.jpeg\"><img width=\"1000\" height=\"1000\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-top.jpeg\" alt=\"Selle Royal Nothing to Hide Saddle top\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-top.jpeg 1000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-top-297x297.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-top-120x120.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-top-768x768.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-top-900x900.jpeg 900w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p>It’s also, let’s be honest, a saddle you can see right through, that lands somewhere between “engineering showcase” and “something you’d rather not discuss after a questionable gas-station burrito.” Or one of these <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/beyond-the-bike-testing-the-best-of-the-worst-tacos-burger-king-vs-jack-in-the-box/\" target=\"_blank\">tacos</a>. Obviously, with the Stracciatella name, they’re going after the classic gelato flavor with shards of chocolate, but there’s something about that yellowish base that is odd, to say the least. </p>\n\n\n\n<p>Selle Royal is selling it in limited quantities, exclusively on its own website, in special anniversary packaging.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-packaging-e1795461736860.jpeg\"><img width=\"1024\" height=\"898\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-packaging-e1795461736860.jpeg\" alt=\"Selle Royal Nothing to Hide Saddle packaging\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-packaging-e1795461736860.jpeg 1024w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-packaging-e1795461736860-297x260.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-packaging-e1795461736860-120x105.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-packaging-e1795461736860-768x674.jpeg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>The Exhibition</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The exhibition took the “Nothing to hide” idea literally. Visitors got a look at failed prototypes and materials that didn’t behave the way engineers expected, which is a refreshing change from an industry that normally only shows you the one thing that worked. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-table-and-chairs.jpeg\"><img width=\"800\" height=\"800\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-table-and-chairs.jpeg\" alt=\"Selle Royal Nothing to Hide Saddle table and chairs\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-table-and-chairs.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-table-and-chairs-297x297.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-table-and-chairs-120x120.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-table-and-chairs-768x768.jpeg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Also on display were artworks from Università Iuav di Venezia design students made from leftover production materials, transparent Stracciatella saddles on custom steel structures, and armchairs made from Stracciatella foam. Yes, you could sit on the foam made from saddle scraps. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-saddle-scraps.jpeg\"><img width=\"800\" height=\"800\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-saddle-scraps.jpeg\" alt=\"Selle Royal Nothing to Hide Saddle saddle scraps\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-saddle-scraps.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-saddle-scraps-297x297.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-saddle-scraps-120x120.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-saddle-scraps-768x768.jpeg 768w\" /></a><figcaption>Saddle waste</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Stracciatella is Selle Royal’s tech for recovering production waste and turning it into new saddle padding. The Lookin Evo’s development also used life cycle assessment to guide design and material choices, which ties the whole thing to the brand’s environmental work.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-mold.jpeg\"><img width=\"800\" height=\"800\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-mold.jpeg\" alt=\"Selle Royal Nothing to Hide Saddle mold\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-mold.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-mold-297x297.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-mold-120x120.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-mold-768x768.jpeg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-tools.jpeg\"><img width=\"800\" height=\"800\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-tools.jpeg\" alt=\"Selle Royal Nothing to Hide Saddle tools\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-tools.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-tools-297x297.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-tools-120x120.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-tools-768x768.jpeg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>70 Years Supporting Your Booty</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The brand has been around for 70 years. Riccardo Bigolin founded Selle Royal in 1956 in the province of Vicenza. By 1960, most of its output was heading to European markets. Along the way came polyurethane foams, Royal Vacuum technology, and Royalgel in 1990. The mission today is still “Support Cyclists.”</p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-modlers-clay.jpeg\"><img width=\"800\" height=\"800\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-modlers-clay.jpeg\" alt=\"Selle Royal Nothing to Hide Saddle modler's clay\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-modlers-clay.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-modlers-clay-297x297.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-modlers-clay-120x120.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-modlers-clay-768x768.jpeg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-displaay.jpeg\"><img width=\"800\" height=\"800\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-displaay.jpeg\" alt=\"Selle Royal Nothing to Hide Saddle displaay\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-displaay.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-displaay-297x297.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-displaay-120x120.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Selle-Royal-Nothing-to-Hide-Saddle-displaay-768x768.jpeg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Seventy years in the saddle business, and the big flex is “look at all the stuff that didn’t work.” Honestly, I respect that approach. I mean, most brands would rather bury the failures in a landfill than put them in a gallery with a DJ. Just don’t expect me to explain the see-through cover to my riding pals.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><em><a href=\"https://www.selleroyal.com/en-us\" target=\"_blank\">SelleRoyal.com</a></em></p>","author":"Ron Frazelle","comments":"https://bikerumor.com/selle-royal-turns-70-with-a-see-through-saddle-and-a-shrine-to-failed-prototypes/#comments","siteTitle":"Bikerumor","siteHash":"49f427af0a926f4232eb837006841d7242e153e3afbb590f32e4b104ea3e2718","entryHash":"73e2cf009ec49386f4a762d0fcf11b2015d7dd2189a57e18a2f25e165831432a","category":"Cycling"}